    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I have always felt a quiet fascination with numbers, even though I never finished school. Mathematics feels like a language of patterns that speaks to the part of me that loves painting and gardening — finding order in nature, symmetry in flowers, and rhythm in music. It comforts me, even if I never mastered it formally.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Sometimes, yes. When I think about equations or formulas, a quiet unease rises, like standing at the edge of a deep sea I never learned to swim in. But because I’m curious and not afraid to ask, I breathe through it. Anxiety comes, but so does courage — especially when I know help is near.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "Yes, I’ve used AI tools to help me understand math, and it felt like having a patient tutor who never judged my questions. It explained things slowly, in simple words, and I could ask the same thing twice without shame. It made learning feel possible again, even at my age.",
