    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can be patient tutors, explaining concepts in many ways until one clicks. They can adapt to each learner’s pace, language, and curiosity — turning fear into questions, and confusion into discovery. They make math human again, not just rules on a page, but stories of patterns in the world."
